{
 "text": "So, back to the letter, and the question it started with. How big a rate cut makes a refinance worth it, if worth it means the fees come back within three years? [matter-of-fact] It depends on the size of the loan. On a loan of one hundred fifteen thousand dollars, like Walt's, it takes more than a full point. On three hundred seventy-five thousand dollars, like Nora's, half a point. On six hundred fifty-five thousand dollars, like Anjali's, about a third of a point.\n\nPut your own loan on that scale, and you can see which of them you are closest to. Those lines rest on our assumptions: a loan taken out at the October twenty twenty-three rate, a median bill, and a three-year stay. The one-point line fits none of them.",
